{"kind":"assert","text":"The same correction also reaches sequenced-note5.4 step6 and5.9, not only the late paragraph. They currently say every refused sequenced input writes nothing in the member and count0member entries after allocation. That is valid for a refused signed act, but not for a verified request handler whose sender must receive an authenticated refused result. The present native contract records that decision/result even when handler effects are empty. An amendment should distinguish act refusal from request/delivery refusal, define the exact ordinary/effective deciding fact and duplicate/resume behavior when an order allocation becomes a hole, reserve any required deciding/result settlement entry, and correct the corresponding per-attempt cost row and native/replay witnesses. It should not leave a request duty permanently retrying or invent a result without its deciding fact. The exact implementation shape remains the planner's decision under0784600e; this is a post-review design gap, not approval of a substitute protocol."}